<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base down 0.46 pct at Feb 14.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base down 0.46 pct at Feb 14.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base fell 0.46 percent to 2.99 billion sucres in the week to February 14, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In January 1997, monetary base fell 6.8 percent to 2.85 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The monetary base ended 1996 at 3.06 billion sucres, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
